<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15183" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-dūro</span></b> , āre,
		1, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>Neut.</i>, <i>to last out</i>, <i>continue</i>, <i>endure</i>
			(post-Aug. and very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solis fulgor in ortus edurat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. G.
					45</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ulla effigies litterarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 14, 1, 18</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to harden</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 11, 1,
				7</span></i>.</div>
